WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:09.670
Explosive Shoot

00:00:16.490 --> 00:00:19.810
Keep fighting chasing your dream

00:00:19.810 --> 00:00:23.140
with love, courage and friendship

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:26.640
This Blade and I are one

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.680
Spin as hard as you can until the limit

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.780
BURNING SOUL

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:46.200
The things I can't do alone

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.140
are not impossible if you're with me

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.960
Come with me

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.280
to the ends of this world

00:00:58.070 --> 00:01:03.540
The Four Sacred Beasts are athletes of love

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:07.100
Shine! Open your eyes!

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.730
Dragoon  Dranzer  Draciel  Driger

00:01:09.730 --> 00:01:12.450
Awaken!

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:16.060
Fly across the sky, my energy

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.380
Rise up, Sacred Beast!

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:22.830
To defeat all the enemies who stand in our way

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:26.050
jump, bearing everyone's hopes

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.080
SHINING SOUL

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.490
The world tournament is finally here.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:45.470
I bet you're looking forward to finding out who we'll be up against, right Takao?

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:53.930
What's wrong, Takao?

00:01:53.930 --> 00:01:55.820
Do I even need to say it?

00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:59.910
I was so hype about this, but we've been on this plane for who knows how many hours.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.250
When the heck are we gonna get there?!

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:07.750
Hey now, think about it. Compared to China, America is much father away from Japan.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:11.880
If you're so bored, why not
read a book or play some games?

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:17.670
I see you already thought of that.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.410
Those two sure are relaxed.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:26.620
The way I see it, Kai is preparing psychologically for the upcoming battles,

00:02:26.620 --> 00:02:28.190
and Max is...

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:35.170
That's America!

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.630
We're here at last, America!

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:41.180
Soon... Soon I'l be able to see you.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:45.190
Mama...

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:50.150
Landing Onto a New Battlefield!

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:55.200
Whoa...

00:02:55.430 --> 00:02:57.860
I'd expect no less from America.

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:04.560
According to my calculations, this building alone can house five times the population of our city.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:05.630
For real?!

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:10.320
Say, want to climb all the way to the top floor? The view must be sweet up there.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.620
Don't get carried away.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:16.090
We didn't come here to play. We're here to fight at the world tournament.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:18.170
Tsk! I already know that.

00:03:18.170 --> 00:03:20.110
I want to see my Mama!

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:24.020
We came all the way here to America,
I want to go see my Mama!

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:27.240
My Mama works as an University professor.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:31.970
That's right, Max was looking
forward to meeting his mother.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:34.370
This should be fine, right Kai?

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:35.100
Foolish.

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:37.680
What?! You didn't have to put it that way!

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:45.530
Well, now. The truth is, the president has instructed me to take you to a certain place.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.380
The old man Daitenji did?

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:50.050
It should be here any minute now.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:51.920
Oh, there it is!

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:55.860
Wow, he came prepared for everything.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:03.090
Grandpa?!

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:05.620
Long time no see, Takao.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:09.800
'Long time'? I was with you until I left Japan!

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:11.650
Why are you here?

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:15.250
He came here to cheer for our team.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:18.690
Yeah but <i>how</i>?! Did he fly
on a UFO or something?!

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:25.030
Thanks to President Daitenji's help,
I came here with a non-stop express flight.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:30.100
I already knew that you would let your guard down in a showy place like America.

00:04:30.100 --> 00:04:32.710
I will be here to keep you focused!

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.600
<i>Oh! Great!</i>

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.560
Why thank you, thank you.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:48.100
What is going on?

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:51.310
Whatever, can you hurry up and get in?

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:51.980
Rei!

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:56.260
I came here before you,
so I'm tired of waiting.

00:04:56.260 --> 00:05:01.700
The place we'll be visiting now is a a staple for anyone who calls themselves a Blader.

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:03.630
Come on, hurry and get in.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:04.580
Yeah.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.680
I can even do this.

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:10.620
Grandpa!

00:05:19.270 --> 00:05:23.260
This is great. Those people were completely entranced by my techniques.

00:05:24.190 --> 00:05:26.280
That was really <i>great</i>!

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:30.270
I want to see it one more time!
Tsk. The giddiest one here is you, Grandpa.

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:31.550
Thank goodness.

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:35.980
We should make it in time for
the appointment. I can't wait.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:40.280
What is it you can't wait for?
Where are you taking us?

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:43.470
Well, you see...

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:46.540
There it is!

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.070
What's <i>that</i>?!

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:49.120
What?

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:53.820
That's the Sacred Land for all Beyblade researchers, the PPB Research Centre!

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:55.500
PPB..?

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:58.620
Project Power of Beyblade.

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:02.860
As the name implies, this ambitious project studies the power of Beyblades

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:06.880
aiming to advance its development
and discover its full potential.

00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:10.180
<i>That's </i>a Beyblade research centre?

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:16.050
Thanks to President Daitenji, we were allowed to take a tour of the facility.

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:18.480
This is a one in a lifetime opportunity!

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.730
The whole place looks showy.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:30.600
The security is stricter than I imagined. As expected from the world-famous PPB.

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:32.340
What do you mean?

00:06:32.340 --> 00:06:37.510
The PPB is one of the national projects that are receiving the most funds by he US government.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:42.000
In other words, what we're about to see is top secret!

00:06:42.370 --> 00:06:44.310
Top secret?!

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:49.840
<i>Welcome!</i> It's great to see you all.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:54.860
I'm Jeff McKenzie, the Vice Director
of the PPB Educational Center.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:56.860
<i>N-Nice to meet you.</i>

00:06:57.120 --> 00:06:58.880
<i>M-my n-name is.. ah</i>

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:00.360
Why are you so nervous?

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:03.600
Mr. Daitenji already told me everything.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:08.360
The Director is currently in a
meeting, so I will be your guide.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:09.850
Please, this way.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:18.630
Aerodynamics, aeronautical engineering...
This research center has gathered experts from all fields,

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:24.530
all to advance the research of Beyblade. This is what the Project Power of Beyblade is about.

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:30.590
Everyday, we try to bring out the potential of Beyblade in cooperation with NASA and the Pentagon.

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:32.230
Let's begin here.

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:35.610
This is the PPB Research Center.

00:07:35.980 --> 00:07:41.230
As you can see, many staff members are conducting scientific research on Beyblade.

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:42.820
Amazing!

00:07:42.820 --> 00:07:47.920
Whoa! All these scientists studying a single Bey.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:49.750
No, it's not 'one Bey'.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.000
It's 'One part of a Beyblade'.

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:55.330
What?! Then, this must mean..!

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:59.380
This section focuses on studying the Blade Base only.

00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:01.840
As for the other parts, come this way.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.270
R-Right!

00:08:03.270 --> 00:08:05.510
Here we have the Spin Gear.

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:07.270
The Weight Disk is here.

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:08.380
Incredible!

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:11.780
And here we research the Attack Ring.

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:13.040
<i>Bravo!</i>

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:17.600
Of course, we are conducting similar research on Shooters and Stadiums as well.

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:25.330
The data acquired here gets sent to the Development Center. Thus, the PPB creates the best Beyblades in the world.

00:08:25.330 --> 00:08:30.250
<i>Even I </i>didn't know about the existence of such a huge research establishment.

00:08:30.250 --> 00:08:32.230
Yeah, I'm flabbergasted.

00:08:32.230 --> 00:08:35.040
I <i>am</i> flabbergasted, but...
I don't know.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:36.290
You don't know..?

00:08:36.290 --> 00:08:40.490
The PPB team is doing some amazing research on Beyblade, that I understand.

00:08:40.490 --> 00:08:45.780
But you know, isn't there more to Beyblade than that?
Sure, research is important, but...

00:08:45.780 --> 00:08:49.850
What about the spirit or the
force of will, that kind of stuff?

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:51.440
Well said, Takao.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:54.670
Right, Grandpa?
Right, Professor?

00:08:57.200 --> 00:08:59.250
W-What are you doing..?

00:09:00.130 --> 00:09:03.540
I'm begging you! Please let me work here!

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:05.770
Dish washing, cleaning, I'll do anything!

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:06.740
Professor!

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:09.660
This place is like a paradise for me.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:15.830
This is a utopia for all those
who live to research Beyblade!

00:09:15.840 --> 00:09:17.380
Please!

00:09:17.380 --> 00:09:18.480
Professor!

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:21.150
Professor sure is in high spirits.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:22.290
Max?

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:26.120
Mama!

00:09:29.650 --> 00:09:31.680
Max..? Is that you, Max?

00:09:33.520 --> 00:09:36.020
Mama!

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:36.890
- Max!

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:39.890
That woman is Max's mother?

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:42.390
I missed you so much, Mama!

00:09:42.730 --> 00:09:45.440
I missed you too, Max. But...

00:09:45.760 --> 00:09:48.080
But why are you here, Mama?

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:50.640
Weren't you working as an University professor?

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:56.580
I'll introduce you. This is the
Director, Doctor Judy Mizuhara.

00:09:58.220 --> 00:09:59.860
Mama, <i>you're</i> the Director?!

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:01.390
Yes.

00:10:01.820 --> 00:10:06.370
Max, your Mom's research was a cornerstone for the development of Bey.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:10.290
And that's why the PPB scouted her talent and hired her.

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:11.620
Director,

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:14.640
this is the BBA team.

00:10:16.140 --> 00:10:17.150
BBA...

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:23.140
Max, you're also part of this BBA team, right?

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:27.570
That's right! I have fought my way here all so that I could meet you again, Mama!

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:30.360
I see...

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:32.490
She's beautiful!

00:10:32.490 --> 00:10:36.020
U-Uhm, we were invited here by President Daitenji...

00:10:36.020 --> 00:10:37.420
Yes, I heard all about it.

00:10:38.190 --> 00:10:45.680
A team that has kept winning relying only on their instincts, with no scientific basis, would come here to visit.

00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:46.660
Mama!

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:50.090
What's this? I don't like her attitude one bit.

00:10:50.550 --> 00:10:53.150
Thanks, Jeff. I'll take over from here.

00:10:54.350 --> 00:10:56.430
Everybody, thanks for waiting.

00:10:56.890 --> 00:11:00.980
From here onward, my assistant
Emily and I will be your guides.

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:06.510
Mama!

00:11:09.470 --> 00:11:17.090
I think you already know this, but using scientific methods to study the potential of Beyblades is our policy here at the PPB.

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:21.280
In other words, our way of thinking is the opposite of the BBA team's.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:26.760
You can research Beys all you want, but the ones playing are still humans...

00:11:26.760 --> 00:11:29.660
Not bad at all. Takao Kinomiya, was it?

00:11:29.910 --> 00:11:31.950
W-Well, uhm...

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:36.260
Indeed, the ones to bring out
a Bey's power are humans.

00:11:36.260 --> 00:11:37.970
That's why...

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:42.640
..we are also putting effort in training Bladers as well.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:44.700
<i>Wow!</i>

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:46.240
Whoa!

00:11:46.240 --> 00:11:49.600
I've never seen a training room this big!

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:59.200
Here we practice a special program to develop the individual dormant potential of excelling and idiosyncratic Bladers.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:04.740
Our computers keep in check their nutrition, health, and even their mental state.

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:06.050
Oh, and of course...

00:12:06.440 --> 00:12:08.540
Paul, your shoot was weak.

00:12:11.580 --> 00:12:13.540
...we also instruct them directly.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:17.150
Magnificent! Truly magnificent!

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:22.590
What do you think, Takao? This is truly the ultimate training center for Bladers!

00:12:23.870 --> 00:12:25.680
What's the big deal?

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:29.090
We're way stronger then them, no doubts about it.

00:12:29.090 --> 00:12:30.900
Want to give it a try?

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:33.480
A battle against us.

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:48.800
Want to give it a try? A battle against us.

00:12:49.060 --> 00:12:50.450
Battle..?

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:52.930
Aren't you Mama's assistant?

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:59.340
Emily <i>is</i> my assistant, but she's also one of the best tennis players in America.

00:13:01.360 --> 00:13:04.290
Not to mention, she's also an Elite Blader of PPB.

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:06.060
Elite Blader?

00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:08.720
Well, feel like playing now?

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:11.430
Cool! I'm getting excited.

00:13:13.090 --> 00:13:16.360
Tony, Andy, please wait there.

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:18.320
Everybody else, you're free to go.

00:13:18.320 --> 00:13:20.500
Remember to complete your final checks.

00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:24.950
Those two plus Emily will fight against you.

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:28.290
As for your team, let's see...

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:32.320
You look strong.

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:34.000
I have no interest in a small fry.

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:35.540
I'll go!

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:36.870
Let's do this, Rei.

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:39.400
I'm not the kind to refuse a battle.

00:13:39.400 --> 00:13:40.020
Max.

00:13:41.610 --> 00:13:43.820
What's going on, Mama?

00:13:43.820 --> 00:13:48.220
You've suddenly become so distant and cold. Why is that?

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:50.890
Please, go to the training room.

00:13:51.520 --> 00:13:53.100
Mama!

00:13:55.280 --> 00:13:57.090
<i>Hey!</i> Who are these guys?

00:13:57.090 --> 00:14:00.630
Apparently, they're the BBA team. They won the Asian qualifiers.

00:14:01.140 --> 00:14:03.490
BBA? Never heard of 'em.

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:05.420
The match will have three rounds.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:07.920
The first to win two rounds will win the match.

00:14:07.920 --> 00:14:09.750
Okay, let's begin.

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:12.450
Alright! I'll go first!

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:15.920
Oh well, I guess I'll start things off.

00:14:18.810 --> 00:14:19.810
What's <i>that</i>?!

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:27.260
A special program to develop the
individual dormant potential...

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:31.480
That peculiar Shooter must
have something to do with that.

00:14:34.340 --> 00:14:36.280
<i>First battle. Ready?</i>

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:39.950
<i>Three, Two, One.</i>

00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:42.490
<i>Go... Shoot!</i>

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:45.520
Go, Dragoon!

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:50.530
What? It jumped?!

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:58.880
<i>Hey, yo!</i> Listen to me, Japanese brother! It would be better for you if away you ran!

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:02.560
Get your things and leave, with your tail between your legs! <i>Go to your home!</i>

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.580
W-What's going on?

00:15:04.580 --> 00:15:10.050
It's rap! I see,
Tony's dormant talent is rap music!

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:13.980
He's making the Bey respond according to the natural rhythm he's producing.

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:17.390
Crap! I can't get a hit like this.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.840
<i>Now attack!</i>

00:15:22.780 --> 00:15:24.350
Get a grip, Dragoon!

00:15:24.350 --> 00:15:26.000
You gotta counterattack!

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:30.610
W-Why you little..!

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:33.620
Don't get hasty, Takao!

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:38.160
If you just calm down, you should be able to easily see through those movements.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:45.090
<i>Hey, hey! Come on, brother!</i>

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:50.250
What's wrong, yo?
Why are you not coming at me, <i>country boy</i>?

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.420
Now, Dragoon!

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:57.350
<i>No!</i>

00:15:59.520 --> 00:16:01.730
Alright! And that's one down!

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:05.560
Well, what do you think
about my Takao? Not bad, is he?

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:08.740
S-Sorry.

00:16:08.740 --> 00:16:11.330
Your Bey is still not in sync with the rhythm.

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:14.260
Andy, please don't mess up.

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:15.960
I know, I know.

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:18.100
<i>Nice attack</i>, Takao.

00:16:18.100 --> 00:16:20.040
That was nothing! Just a warm up!

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:23.570
I wonder, it looked to me like
you were struggling out there.

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:25.380
Well, then, I'm going next.

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:30.760
Thaat's quite a cute Bey you've got there.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.650
It's <i>art</i>.

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:34.520
It's psychedelic.

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:36.880
Second battle.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:38.350
Ready?

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:41.050
Three, Two, One.

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:42.940
Go... Shoot!

00:16:56.000 --> 00:16:57.370
What's the deal with that?!

00:16:57.370 --> 00:16:59.160
I-It's pop art!

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:02.320
One of the styles created in America.

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:05.690
I see, his dormant talent is art!

00:17:05.690 --> 00:17:09.630
His artistic sense is being materialized through his Bey.

00:17:10.630 --> 00:17:11.470
It vanished?!

00:17:11.470 --> 00:17:17.680
That's right. The PPB's scientific power lets us make use of any talent for Beyblade.

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:21.880
I had no idea such an unusual strategy could exist.

00:17:23.110 --> 00:17:25.980
Well, what do you think about
my <i>art</i>? <i>Beautiful</i>, isn't it?

00:17:26.500 --> 00:17:32.110
Oh yeah, I remember a Blader in the Nepal mountains used a similar deception.

00:17:32.110 --> 00:17:33.120
What?!

00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:37.620
I traveled across the world, and fought against all sorts of opponents.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:40.540
A childish trick like this won't work on me!

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:43.160
Go, Driger!

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:52.090
It's over for you.

00:17:54.980 --> 00:17:59.060
Andy, Stadium out. The winner is Rei.

00:17:59.960 --> 00:18:01.640
My <i>art</i>!

00:18:03.300 --> 00:18:06.480
Alright! With this, the match is ours!

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:10.870
What do you think of the power of the team that won the Asian tournament?

00:18:11.640 --> 00:18:13.020
Is the opening act over?

00:18:13.620 --> 00:18:15.320
The real thing starts now.

00:18:16.600 --> 00:18:18.220
Say, Professor.

00:18:18.220 --> 00:18:22.230
I don't know about their scientific power and stuff, but aren't we stronger?

00:18:22.230 --> 00:18:23.650
I wonder about that.

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:28.630
Is this really the true power of the PPB?

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:30.570
What the..? What's with you?

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:36.160
Alright Max, it's your turn now! Let's end this with three wins in a row!

00:18:36.160 --> 00:18:37.600
Leave it to me!

00:18:40.310 --> 00:18:41.720
Let's have a good fight, Max.

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:43.260
Same to you.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:58.150
Emily, where is your Shooter?

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:00.230
This is all I need.

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:02.720
That's a tennis racket-shaped Shooter!

00:19:02.720 --> 00:19:03.840
<i>Wow!</i>

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:05.810
So what?

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:08.290
<i>Final battle. Ready?</i>

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:11.740
Three, Two, One...

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:14.340
Go... Shoot!

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:21.540
Her dormant talent is tennis.

00:19:21.540 --> 00:19:23.100
The problem is her power.

00:19:23.100 --> 00:19:25.070
I'll show you my power!

00:19:25.070 --> 00:19:27.070
Go, Drigator!

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:29.850
Shake it off, Draciel!

00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:34.480
<i>No!</i>

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:42.910
Max, Stadium out.

00:19:43.130 --> 00:19:45.000
The winner is Emily.

00:19:45.400 --> 00:19:47.280
What amazing power.

00:19:47.280 --> 00:19:52.560
She managed to defeat Draciel, who went though countless revisions, in one single attack.

00:19:52.560 --> 00:19:54.750
That girl... is not your average Blader.

00:19:55.530 --> 00:19:56.840
That's a service ace.

00:19:58.370 --> 00:20:00.280
My poor Draciel...

00:20:00.280 --> 00:20:04.230
Don't feel down. Either way, our team won this match.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:07.550
We successfully proved to them that Beyblade is about your spirit.

00:20:07.550 --> 00:20:09.150
Did we really?

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:12.180
What we did until now didn't prove anything.

00:20:12.180 --> 00:20:13.030
What?

00:20:13.030 --> 00:20:14.150
Am I wrong, Emily?

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:19.400
No, you're right. The ones you fought against were the PPB second string players.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:21.330
Second string players?!

00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:23.310
Let me explain.

00:20:23.310 --> 00:20:27.880
The American representative team that you will face at the World tournament

00:20:27.880 --> 00:20:31.160
is made of the Elite players born here at the PPB research center.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:35.120
Tony and Andy are second string players who didn't make the cut.

00:20:35.640 --> 00:20:37.840
Of course I'm not like them.

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:42.760
I don't like this one bit. Why did you have us fight against your second string players?

00:20:42.760 --> 00:20:47.600
Don't you think that using players from the first string just to gather data is a waste of time?

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:52.210
Now we have a rough idea of your dormant talents.

00:20:52.210 --> 00:20:54.720
So you <i>were</i> gathering data. I knew it.

00:20:54.720 --> 00:20:57.620
But how? Where are the computers?

00:20:58.300 --> 00:20:59.150
Right here.

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:00.490
Magnificent!

00:21:00.490 --> 00:21:01.840
Don't admire them!

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:03.110
It may sound rude,

00:21:03.110 --> 00:21:07.720
but your level of skill was
nothing out of our expectations.

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:11.800
So the BBA team will <i>never</i> be able
to win against the PPB team.

00:21:12.310 --> 00:21:17.200
Spirit and will force can't
compete with the power of science.

00:21:17.200 --> 00:21:18.200
Mama...

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:24.650
What's her deal?! I stayed quiet because she's Max's Mom, but if she keeps running her mouth like that any longer..!

00:21:24.650 --> 00:21:31.730
Just you wait! I don't know about the PPB first string players, but we're gonna win no matter what!

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:44.720
Spring waves its hand smiling,

00:21:44.720 --> 00:21:50.200
Summer spreads passion.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:55.350
Seasons pass one after the other,

00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:59.560
Fall and Winter are good friends.

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:05.660
When there is a problem you can't solve,

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:11.560
Trust, friendship, love and emotion

00:22:14.120 --> 00:22:18.800
Clouds keep flying across the sky,

00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:24.200
the sky keeps changing every second

00:22:24.200 --> 00:22:29.090
My eyes well up and tears stream down my face,

00:22:29.090 --> 00:22:33.090
but they're not tears of sadness

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:39.420
I summon my courage and try to put it into words.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:44.770
"Let's go on a journey to the city of hope!"

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:49.760
All your dreams will come true

00:22:57.620 --> 00:23:01.960
According to my analysis, Max's mother has a natural talent for science.

00:23:01.960 --> 00:23:04.820
That ice-cold stare of hers is wonderful!

00:23:04.820 --> 00:23:10.960
I also want to see what's inside the PPB's secret structures... Which is why I snuck in.

00:23:11.160 --> 00:23:16.580
Waiting there was none other than one of the PPB team's first string members!

00:23:16.920 --> 00:23:19.600
Next time: The Fearsome <i>American Power</i>!

00:23:20.030 --> 00:23:24.990
Ah! That's the Sacred Beast of the Buffalo!
This is going to be tough!
